  "answer": "Operators must implement necessary compensating measures to maintain a prudent/satisfactory level of health, safety and the environment when safety barriers are missing or impaired, and when nonconformities have not yet been corrected. Compensatory measures for impaired safety systems shall be set in advance and implemented as rapidly/as soon as possible when impairment occurs. Operators must also ensure corrective actions, identify causes and implement remedial and preventive measures for nonconformities, and follow up and evaluate effects; until correction, necessary compensating measures shall be implemented. Additionally, the status of safety systems and nonconformities shall be known and available to relevant personnel and maintained in an overview by the operator.",
